# Pages and routing

**Multi-page, not a SPA.** Each route is a real HTML file that loads its own mount
script. There is no router and no client-side navigation. Deep links resolve as static
files, which is why `404.html` can stay a genuine error page instead of an SPA redirect
shim (ADR-0002).

## Every HTML entry point must have

- `<title>` and `<meta name="description">` specific to the page
- `<link rel="canonical">` pointing at the **apex** `https://nalam.me/...` — matching
  `CNAME`. Never `www.` (ADR-0003)
- The inline theme bootstrap script — sets `.dark` on `<html>` before first paint. Omit
  it and the page flashes light before going dark
- `<div id="root">` and a module script pointing at `/entries/<name>.tsx`
- `og:` tags. These are the only content crawlers see without executing JS, so they
  matter more here than on a server-rendered site

Only `src/index.html` carries the `Person` JSON-LD block.

## Component structure

- `Page` wraps every route: header, `<main>`, footer. Pass `back` on subpages for the
  "← Nazmul Alam" link
- `Section` is the layout unit — `max-w-3xl`, consistent padding, optional small-caps title
- `CaseStudyPage` renders any case study from its slug; the four subpages differ only by
  that slug. Content comes from `caseStudies` in `src/content/site.ts` — do not hardcode
  prose in the component

## Accessibility

- The hero image is decorative (`alt=""`) because the `<h1>` beneath it already
  announces the name. Do not "fix" this by adding alt text
- Keep the visible focus ring in `globals.css`
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — already handled in the base layer
